        <body>
            <div xml:id="d744">

                <pb facs="0640" n="628" xml:id="pg628"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/257: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Burdett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-11-18T19:00:00-05:00">November 18, 1940—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>402. From the Ambassador. Your 593, November 16, 4 p.m. Please tell Aranha that
                    the Acting Secretary and I have both been pressing this matter continually at
                    the British Embassy here during the past fortnight. I am to speak on the subject
                    again with the British Chargé d’Affaires this afternoon. [Caffery.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
